                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2a417808-7c76-4740-b851-812cd39a285b",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e6bbe07-87dd-35fb-a43d-ccd3211fd92c",
                        "source_sense_id": "8a0d5f4a-3ccb-3fed-b99a-8e27086eee80",
                        "target_lang_word": "butyrate",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "butyrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "3f625460-554d-3222-b7b0-9da7f7a7a1a5",
                                        "entry_id": "805e31ff-59d9-3e83-bbb0-071765b1a166",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any salt or ester of butyric acid."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "52cef9b1-690a-4063-a9f8-924355e098a9",
                                                "sense_id": "3f625460-554d-3222-b7b0-9da7f7a7a1a5",
                                                "text": "It is butyrate, however, which is the fatty acid of most importance to the colonic epithelial cell. Apart from being an important respiratory fuel for the colonocyte, butyrate has remarkably diverse properties in a wide range of cells."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "db4445d0-422c-4453-a9cc-de81de52e684",
                                                "sense_id": "3f625460-554d-3222-b7b0-9da7f7a7a1a5",
                                                "text": "Another question to be raised is the possible use of butyrate in the lipogenic pathway. Even though the carbons from butyrate could be incorporated into lipid extracts [12], this incorporation represents less than 1 % of CO₂, and TKB productions."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "81daa96c-609a-462b-9e8a-bd7ecbcdfe94",
                                                "sense_id": "3f625460-554d-3222-b7b0-9da7f7a7a1a5",
                                                "text": "To examine the effects of sodium butyrate on virus production, cells were exposed to sodium butyrate at various concentrations and times starting 16 h after transfection."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0c4bd27a-c5f2-441f-925c-2f9f0cb39922",
                                                "sense_id": "3f625460-554d-3222-b7b0-9da7f7a7a1a5",
                                                "text": "Butyrates are four carbon fatty acids first found in butter. Butyrates are formed naturally in the gut by friendly bacteria (probiotics) digesting fibre, such as the fibre in psyllium seed husks."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "798af35e-5995-4ce1-bc8a-be0cad5f9433",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e6bbe07-87dd-35fb-a43d-ccd3211fd92c",
                        "source_sense_id": "8a0d5f4a-3ccb-3fed-b99a-8e27086eee80",
                        "target_lang_word": "máselnan",
                        "target_lang_code": "cs",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "máselnan",
                                "target_lang_code": "cs",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "5f97daec-bd14-3f73-9890-e083d3b3961b",
                                        "entry_id": "801a9e10-78df-3370-bbea-cae1751fec48",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "sůl nebo ester kyseliny máselné"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3b0c4aa8-1932-421e-a46e-42f3bd2f0038",
                                                "sense_id": "5f97daec-bd14-3f73-9890-e083d3b3961b",
                                                "text": "Vyvíjí-li se máselnan ethylnatý (pozná se zápachem), domnívati se můžeme, že jest buď přírodní nebo uměle pomíšeno; nevyvíjí-li se máselnan, jest to máslo umělé."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "7f9a5d36-436c-41c6-af67-bfcc8fb3d6ef",
                        "source_entry_id": "3e6bbe07-87dd-35fb-a43d-ccd3211fd92c",
                        "source_sense_id": "8a0d5f4a-3ccb-3fed-b99a-8e27086eee80",
                        "target_lang_word": "butyrate",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "butyrate",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2d3de754-97bd-33cd-b97a-4c6955b591e6",
                                        "entry_id": "8f9dd514-a81a-31aa-8b27-2fcaef978c39",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Nom des sels formés avec l’acide butyrique et une base."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "98e9cba0-d972-42ee-9f99-6014d6c958da",
                                                "sense_id": "2d3de754-97bd-33cd-b97a-4c6955b591e6",
                                                "text": "Sur des suspensions de colonocytes humains in vitro, le butyrate est oxydé préférentiellement par rapport au glucose et à la glutamine."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "93b6d5d7-3c84-497b-8e02-278ed9709a4b",
                                                "sense_id": "2d3de754-97bd-33cd-b97a-4c6955b591e6",
                                                "text": "Les butyrates de cellulose ont une gamme de solubilité plus étendue que les acétates; c’est ainsi qu’ils sont solubles dans les solvants usuels tels que le mélange alcool-benzène."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
